  const rule=document.createElement('div');rule.className='lowfield-rule';rule.innerHTML='<b>Signal and dephasing conventions.</b> Panel B is one continuously sampled physical z-line from the central water condition; it is never assembled by alternating scanner conditions. Panels D–F retain the separately solved B<sub>0</sub>, B<sub>1</sub>, water and fat conditions. <span style="color:#E9A23B">Raw slab signal</span> is normalized to equilibrium magnetization of the complete 10 mm voxel. The <span style="color:#4AA8FF">dashed slice-normalized signal</span> divides that same complex sum by its first post-RF1 magnitude.';stage.appendChild(rule);
  const row1=document.createElement('div');row1.className='lowfield-grid';stage.appendChild(row1);const voxel=mkCanvas(row1,650,430,'B · rotatable 3-D magnetization along one continuous physical z-line');const profile=mkCanvas(row1,650,430,'C · condition-averaged slice profile reconstructed from graph states');
